      "name": "invalid null price (bug)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "let res = pm.response.json();\r",
              "\r",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {\r",
              "    pm.test(\"BUG: API accepted null price\", function () {\r",
              "        pm.expect.fail(\"API should reject null price but it accepted it\");\r",
              "    });\r",
              "} else {\r",
              "    pm.test(\"Null price rejected correctly\", function () {\r",
              "        pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(400);\r",
              "    });\r",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {},
            "requests": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\r\n  \"title\": \"Null price\",\r\n  \"price\":null,\r\n  \"description\": \"Null price test\",\r\n  \"category\": \"test\"\r\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products/add",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "products",
            "add"
          ]
        },
        "description": "## Request Tests Documentation\n\nThis request includes automated tests to validate that the API rejects null price values during product creation.\n\n---\n\n### Status Code Validation\n\n• Ensures the API does not return 200 OK or 201 Created for invalid price input.  \n• Confirms the request is properly rejected.\n\n---\n\n### Purpose\n\nThese tests ensure that:  \n• Nullprices are not accepted.  \n• Business rules are enforced.  \n• Invalid data does not result in a successful response.\n\n---\n\n### Notes\n\n• Status code is accessed using pm.response.code.  \n• The test fails if the API accepts a negative price.  \n• Designed for negative testing scenarios."
